WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.380
The most dangerous flea market in Serbia.

2
00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:07.720
Today is a big promotion. Follow six items, get the seventh free.

3
00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:13.800
I found my bag. Is that even possible? That can only happen to me.

4
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.690
Promotion, promotion, promotion.

5
00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:19.300
It's not pleasant when a truck drives around you like this.

6
00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:23.370
Today I'm going to the flea market in Pančevo. It's Sunday.

7
00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:27.670
I'm already late, but I don't think that's so terrible.

8
00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:32.820
I used to come quite late before too, now it's a quarter to twelve.

9
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.860
The goal when I go to a flea market: there is no goal.

10
00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:42.200
I never think about what I'll buy, because that's impossible,

11
00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.790
and things mostly find me.

12
00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:49.720
For some reason I'm lucky with things and I always find something.

13
00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:51.970
Wherever I go.

14
00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:54.620
I don't know, I dress like an action man.

15
00:00:54.620 --> 00:01:00.080
And I always tell my mom: if you dress up for the flea market, they raise the prices on you.

16
00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:07.020
So I look like an action man, but fine, I feel most comfortable, comfort is a must.

17
00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:17.140
The problem with the flea market in Pančevo is that it has no designated space.

18
00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:20.040
This is a wild flea market.

19
00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:32.230
And the residents of Pančevo often write to me that they don't like the flea market much, because it's in the middle of the street, creates a huge crowd, leaves a lot of trash behind.

20
00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:33.290
Here, trash.

21
00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:43.280
Trash is a big problem at any flea market where I've been, there's always some pile where the leftovers get dumped, a catastrophe.

22
00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:52.650
I love Serbia and my country most of all, but if there's something I hate, it's the trash we have, and it's really special.

23
00:01:52.650 --> 00:02:00.600
Especially here with us, at least in Europe, hardly any other country has such a problem with trash.

24
00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:10.470
By the way, this windbreaker jacket is a relatively local brand, let's say from Banja Luka.

25
00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:14.180
It's called Brat Wear and I wear it often.

26
00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:17.570
Just to mention it, it's really cool.

27
00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:19.160
Here's the label.

28
00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:25.200
I have lots of pockets, which is quite important to me, and it's comfortable.

29
00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:28.120
A horror happened: my coffee spilled all over the car.

30
00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:36.820
We'll see, we'll see.

31
00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:38.550
We'll have an ad too.

32
00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:42.000
And what should I say, where can people find you?

33
00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:45.120
Korleone, a Balkan Minecraft server.

34
00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:47.570
Really? What do you do, Korleone?

35
00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:49.010
A Minecraft server.

36
00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:53.480
Oh, so there's that here too. Do you need an ad on YouTube?

37
00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:57.110
Okay, my eyes. See you on YouTube. Bye, boss.

38
00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:20.570
I was looking for a hat, and I found a cap from the Korleone Minecraft server.

39
00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:34.480
You can't even choose and buy in peace when the trucks drive by.

40
00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:42.500
I love jewellery, but here it's rather weak.

41
00:04:54.600 --> 00:05:00.520
I can't believe it, that can only happen to me.

42
00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:13.320
So, I found my bag and it must be my bag, there's no such bag because I made it myself.

43
00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:15.980
I can't believe it.

44
00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:23.830
Boss, is this yours? This is mine, and I threw it away the other day.

45
00:05:23.830 --> 00:05:31.200
I can't believe that it came here now and that I found it.

46
00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:35.790
Do you collect there or what, who brought it to you?

47
00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:41.340
But I can't believe that it was me who found it.

48
00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:48.470
I mean, I don't need it, it's old, but I can't believe it.

49
00:05:48.470 --> 00:05:50.040
It's hilarious.

50
00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:56.840
Well, there's nothing else, but this exists.

51
00:05:56.840 --> 00:06:03.660
The bag is very old, my grandmother even altered it for me, it wasn't even a bag, it was a skirt, a leather one.

52
00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:09.530
Really old, worn out, I threw it away because it can't be sold or given to anyone.

53
00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:11.110
And here I found it at the flea market.

54
00:06:11.110 --> 00:06:12.310
Is that even possible?

55
00:06:13.770 --> 00:06:17.110
There, if somebody wants to upcycle it into a bag.

56
00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:20.840
It's a real upcycle, but it's just no good.

57
00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:25.140
It can't be used, it has no handle, nothing.

58
00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:29.630
Oh, God. What a coincidence! I can't believe it.

59
00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:37.860
Digging, digging, digging.

60
00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:17.880
I can't believe it, I haven't found anything. Yet.

61
00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:21.510
Now we're going off to the side a little.

62
00:07:21.510 --> 00:07:23.330
Juicy Couture.

63
00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:26.310
We don't like skinny jeans.

64
00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:13.860
I haggled over leather trousers, 700 dinars.

65
00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:16.750
Hop, hop, not bad.

66
00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:24.990
Maybe there's something here in the boxes.

67
00:08:24.990 --> 00:08:33.340
There aren't even any dishes, it's all some plastic, some strange things.

68
00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:03.760
I think I'll take it. Let me just see how to pack it.

69
00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:05.200
This coat rack, man.

70
00:10:21.580 --> 00:10:29.520
Look at this. Well, I didn't expect that. Did you say a thousand?

71
00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:37.680
Thanks. Have a nice day. You too.

72
00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:40.680
Coat rack. Secured.

73
00:10:42.380 --> 00:10:45.910
I need the keys to hang on it by the door.

74
00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:50.880
We'll see if it fits, but I like it, metal, maybe brass, I don't know.

75
00:10:56.040 --> 00:11:06.580
They've started packing up, but that's good, because then everyone's leaving and wants to give things away cheap, at the end, to get rid of stuff.

76
00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:19.490
A suitcase, I've been looking for one like this for a thousand years, but it usually ends up overpriced, but it's good.

77
00:11:30.880 --> 00:11:35.430
Boss lady, how much are they?

78
00:11:35.430 --> 00:11:40.490
Four pieces, six hundred.

79
00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:42.510
That's okay.

80
00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:46.020
Candlesticks.

81
00:11:46.020 --> 00:12:02.490
Wait, wait, let me repack so they can fit.

82
00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:12.650
Don't you worry about anything.

83
00:12:12.650 --> 00:12:23.870
Not bad. Everything can fit.

84
00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:50.920
I saw some really good chairs.

85
00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:55.620
They have the potential to be sanded down and fitted with sponge pads.

86
00:12:55.620 --> 00:13:00.400
But I took the man's number, I have to see whether they'll fit for me.

87
00:13:07.600 --> 00:13:10.900
Something pulls me ahead, and I can't see the end.

88
00:13:10.900 --> 00:13:14.620
But yes, mostly it's all some kind of tools now.

89
00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:17.400
These are some plants, that's good.

90
00:13:42.690 --> 00:13:45.270
The most dangerous flea market in Serbia.

91
00:13:45.270 --> 00:13:49.190
It's not pleasant when a truck drives around you like this.

92
00:14:18.340 --> 00:14:24.340
When I think I've reached the end, there's still all of this over there.

93
00:14:36.340 --> 00:14:44.010
These are new things. Oh, wow.

94
00:14:44.010 --> 00:14:53.790
These are some Zara things and H&M things.

95
00:14:53.790 --> 00:14:55.110
New.

96
00:14:55.110 --> 00:15:08.330
I'm looking at it, but this is really cool, I just don't need it.

97
00:15:08.330 --> 00:15:14.680
Yes, this is underwear from H&M.

98
00:15:22.700 --> 00:15:29.780
Springfield, Zara.

99
00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:42.760
But I don't need it, I like this one.

100
00:15:42.760 --> 00:15:51.810
A leather vest, but a small one.

101
00:15:51.810 --> 00:16:00.070
I don't know, I don't need it.

102
00:16:00.070 --> 00:16:20.140
Look, this one is good, if it were a bit thicker. A brown coat.

103
00:16:20.140 --> 00:16:29.580
This is a premium location.

104
00:16:35.400 --> 00:16:48.950
Well, we've found various things.

105
00:16:48.950 --> 00:17:04.050
It depends on the day, sometimes the flea market is better.

106
00:17:04.050 --> 00:17:19.160
It seems to me that now it's all some kind of junk.

107
00:17:19.160 --> 00:17:35.030
I have no idea. Maybe it's simply better in summer.

108
00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:49.360
I really don't need that, I already have four.

109
00:17:51.870 --> 00:17:54.610
Some tips: you have to dig as much as you can.

110
00:17:54.610 --> 00:17:58.810
I, for example, didn't have so much strength today to dig,

111
00:17:58.810 --> 00:18:06.350
but normally I dig through those piles, and I usually notice right away whether there are good things in the pile or not.

112
00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:12.910
You can tell by the labels. If I immediately see some old labels, it means good things are there.

113
00:18:12.910 --> 00:18:17.710
If I see Shein and some new brands, those Chinese ones, I run away right away.

114
00:18:17.710 --> 00:18:21.860
Today I didn't dig so much, but I saw a pro tip:

115
00:18:21.860 --> 00:18:27.410
the Russians have gloves, those rubber cleaning gloves, and they dig with them.

116
00:18:27.410 --> 00:18:36.530
I take leather things to dry cleaning, often I take something in a little, but mostly I see that something has potential

117
00:18:36.530 --> 00:18:42.090
and I hold back from buying too much. So that's the main message.

118
00:18:42.090 --> 00:18:46.190
Well, today I saw a lot of things that I liked, but realistically, what would I need them for?

119
00:18:46.190 --> 00:18:49.270
In the end I took three things, we'll see in the car what exactly.

120
00:18:50.970 --> 00:18:53.550
Next, a tip: haggling.

121
00:18:53.550 --> 00:19:03.520
The first price, no. Usually make an offer, if not, he raises it a bit, but I always manage to get it down a little.

122
00:19:03.520 --> 00:19:05.650
That's the charm of a flea market.

123
00:19:06.570 --> 00:19:11.110
I used to be able to overdo it and take things I don't need.

124
00:19:11.110 --> 00:19:12.940
Now I'm restrained, honestly.

125
00:19:12.940 --> 00:19:20.590
And I need things for the flat or the house more than clothes, although my only weakness is leather things, as you saw.

126
00:19:20.590 --> 00:19:28.520
And I haggled: he asked for a thousand-something, I brought it down to 700; he asked a thousand and a half for the leather trousers.

127
00:19:28.520 --> 00:19:35.590
Well, the good thing is that people often want to be filmed. I find that interesting, and then they ask whether it's for TikTok.

128
00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:46.340
A successful visit to the flea market today.

129
00:19:46.340 --> 00:19:52.310
And this is what I took, which you probably saw.

130
00:19:52.310 --> 00:19:54.650
A brass coat rack,

131
00:19:54.650 --> 00:20:02.040
which will go in front of, that is, next to my entrance door.

132
00:20:02.040 --> 00:20:13.680
And somehow I don't want to put things on it, I imagined the keys hanging there,

133
00:20:13.680 --> 00:20:23.890
and here something like this, blah blah blah, and the keys below, or maybe I'll take it to the garden.

134
00:20:23.890 --> 00:20:26.510
Anyway, I liked it.

135
00:20:26.510 --> 00:20:30.040
Okay. We're satisfied with that.

136
00:20:31.280 --> 00:20:34.890
Next, new unpacked candlesticks.

137
00:20:34.890 --> 00:20:38.290
I have no idea where they're from, it says Germany.

138
00:20:38.290 --> 00:20:40.760
They look like Zara Home.

139
00:20:41.380 --> 00:20:44.540
I make a habit of hunting for Zara Home dupes,

140
00:20:44.540 --> 00:20:50.160
that is, things inspired by Zara Home. This is definitely one of the dupes.

141
00:20:50.220 --> 00:21:00.790
So I think this would cost 300 euros at Zara Home.

142
00:21:00.790 --> 00:21:05.180
Metal, yes, and this black one.

143
00:21:05.180 --> 00:21:08.170
Four pieces, 600 dinars.

144
00:21:08.170 --> 00:21:13.240
At Zara this would cost 20,000, four pieces.

145
00:21:13.240 --> 00:21:20.000
So, new, unpacked; these will probably go to the garden, because everything there for me is black like this.

146
00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:22.680
So most likely these are going there.

147
00:21:22.680 --> 00:21:24.830
This is a really good catch for me.

148
00:21:24.830 --> 00:21:32.420
I especially like this one, and I hadn't found anything so interesting and nice in decorations for a long time.

149
00:21:32.420 --> 00:21:35.740
The last thing I haggled over, they talked me into taking it:

150
00:21:35.740 --> 00:21:39.440
leather trousers. I have no idea whether they'll fit me, they look a little small to me.

151
00:21:44.580 --> 00:21:48.380
By the way, I'm planning to start learning to ride a motorcycle,

152
00:21:48.380 --> 00:21:54.930
but anyway I wear this kind of thing every day. They're small, we'll see whether I fit into them.

153
00:21:54.930 --> 00:21:58.500
If not, I found very interesting things today.

154
00:21:59.060 --> 00:22:05.860
I didn't overdo it, I say again, that's very important to me, I don't want to buy just for the sake of buying something.

155
00:22:05.860 --> 00:22:12.230
I'll use these things, and honestly I'm really glad I took these two things for the house,

156
00:22:12.230 --> 00:22:13.660
and one pair of trousers.

157
00:22:14.380 --> 00:22:21.180
One thing I didn't do this time, but you should: have alcohol for your hands, at least, or some wet wipes,

158
00:22:21.180 --> 00:22:25.040
because my hands are filthy now from everything I touched there.

159
00:22:25.040 --> 00:22:35.850
I make an excursion out of going to a flea market, it's my favourite activity and hobby, I'll never get tired of it.

160
00:22:35.850 --> 00:22:44.360
Maybe I even prefer going around the interior, to some small places, to markets and so on.

161
00:22:45.560 --> 00:22:49.780
This is still a fairly well-known flea market, there are many people, but you saw how chaotic it is:

162
00:22:49.780 --> 00:22:52.400
cars go by, trucks go by, a million people, you watch where you step.

163
00:22:52.400 --> 00:23:02.780
So you have to know what awaits you. It's quite crowded, there's all sorts of things, there's trash,

164
00:23:02.780 --> 00:23:08.400
but there's also something interesting to find.

165
00:23:08.400 --> 00:23:12.780
Quite a few of these sellers have ads on Facebook Marketplace,

166
00:23:12.780 --> 00:23:18.400
and take my word for it, I think Facebook Marketplace is the next big thing.

167
00:23:18.400 --> 00:23:27.210
With us people don't even know that it works: Facebook Marketplace, that section on Facebook where you can post ads.

168
00:23:27.210 --> 00:23:37.360
I sold one Ikea piece, I think. Maybe I'm even better at buying than selling, because it's easier to use, and the prices may be even cheaper.

169
00:23:37.360 --> 00:23:46.540
Abroad it's completely normal to sell on Facebook Marketplace. I know Americans buy a lot of furniture that way,

170
00:23:46.540 --> 00:23:51.320
and people give things away for free. With us nobody wants to give anything for free.

171
00:23:51.320 --> 00:23:59.390
By the way, every first weekend of the month you can also put out some larger waste into the container.

172
00:23:59.390 --> 00:24:06.080
It says so on the official website of the city sanitation service for Belgrade: the first weekend of the month.

173
00:24:06.080 --> 00:24:11.320
But then you throw out some things and find them here, like me today.

174
00:24:11.320 --> 00:24:13.250
That's my impression of the day.

175
00:24:13.250 --> 00:24:21.320
I can't believe that I found my bag there, my bag that I altered myself.

176
00:24:21.320 --> 00:24:27.110
I don't like those prejudices and squeamishness. You take someone else's thing and it carries energy with it.

177
00:24:27.110 --> 00:24:31.320
I think it carries energy only if you give it that energy.

178
00:24:32.320 --> 00:24:35.260
I filmed the trash for you there, of course.

179
00:24:35.260 --> 00:24:41.290
That's of course the bad side of the flea market, but in general this happens here with us everywhere.

180
00:24:41.290 --> 00:24:57.880
It's a catastrophe how much trash people leave behind. Of course it wouldn't be pleasant for me if I were one of the residents in those houses around the flea market, not at all pleasant that so much trash is created there every weekend,

181
00:24:57.880 --> 00:25:02.160
and again that's something the authorities in the city should solve.

182
00:25:02.160 --> 00:25:09.230
So, the flea market must have a designated space, instead of it happening like this, in the middle of the street.

183
00:25:09.230 --> 00:25:15.420
It's terrible. But pressure needs to be put on the authorities to solve such things.

184
00:25:18.300 --> 00:25:19.960
I've told you a lot.

185
00:25:19.960 --> 00:25:23.850
I don't know how long this video will be, I'm really curious.

186
00:25:23.850 --> 00:25:32.580
As always, write to me in the comments what you think about these topics: old things, used, second hand, flea markets and markets.

187
00:25:32.580 --> 00:25:36.760
I like visiting them and I'll gladly film them like this every time.

188
00:25:36.760 --> 00:25:45.700
This is a light format for me: I carry a camera with me, talk about impressions, film on the spot, and I believe you'll like it.

189
00:25:45.700 --> 00:25:50.320
Nothing serious, I save more serious formats for some trips.

190
00:25:51.520 --> 00:25:56.600
Your chosen collector of secondary raw materials, always from this...

191
00:25:56.600 --> 00:26:08.830
Subscribe to the channel, because I'll try every time I go to markets and flea markets like this to film, I'm sure you'll enjoy watching.

192
00:26:08.830 --> 00:26:18.040
That's it for today, we'll talk next time, and we see each other every day on Instagram and TikTok, you already know that. Bye!
